From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: multicolor: honor disabled sysfs ownership for intensity writes

Match the existing brightness and trigger write gates while a kernel consumer
owns the LED. Read-only status remains available.

--- a/drivers/leds/led-class-multicolor.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/led-class-multicolor.c
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&led_cdev->led_access);
 
+	if (led_sysfs_is_disabled(led_cdev)) {
+		ret = -EBUSY;
+		goto err_out;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < mcled_cdev->num_colors; i++) {
 		ret = sscanf(buf + offset, "%u%n",
 			     &intensity_value[i], &nrchars);
